# --- WarpX simulation output (large, machine-specific, regenerable from the decks) ---
runs/**/diags/
# ...and the same path when it is a SYMLINK rather than a directory. A trailing slash
# matches directories only, so once diags/ is archived off the fast disk (e.g. to
# /mnt/cellar) and replaced by a symlink, git stops ignoring it and offers to commit a
# link that resolves nowhere on anyone else's machine.
runs/**/diags
runs/**/diags_movies/
runs/**/diags_movie/

# --- studies scratch (WarpX variant runs, regenerable from the runner) ---
studies/**/scratch/

# --- preserved pre-optimisation WarpX binaries (45 MB, rebuildable from the commit) ---
studies/ray_march_perf/baseline_bin/

# --- any media (figures, movies and their frame scratch: all regenerable) ---
media/

# --- run logs (large with verbose=1; findings are recorded in RESULTS.md) ---
*.log
!progress.log

# --- generated / transient ---
runs/**/config.generated.yaml
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
*.swp

# AMReX backtrace dumps
Backtrace.*

# --- job scratch (regen logs, ad-hoc; keepers live in scripts/) ---
tmp/

# --- progress-logger stdout (the findings live in progress.log / RESULTS.md) ---
runs/**/*.out

# --- PSC laser module ---
psc-raytrace-master.zip
*.pdf
# --- PSC laser module: unreleased/sensitive. Never commit its source, an archive of
# it, an extracted tree, or code derived from it. See
# warpx-cda/laser_deposition/psc_reference/README.md for where PSC-coupled code lives.
psc-raytrace*
PIC_*.f
PIC_*.F90
VLA*.f
VLI*.f
INIT_*.f
studies/psc_absorption_xcheck.py

# --- session worktrees (embedded git repos, not submodules) ---
.claude/worktrees/

# --- aborted/renamed run logs. A voided run's step output is as large as a live one's
# (1 MB here, 40 MB for the valid run) and `*.log` does not match `run.log.<suffix>`.
# Its SMALL siblings are deliberately NOT ignored: warpx_used_inputs.aborted-* is the
# evidence of what the void binary actually parsed, and progress.log.aborted-* is its
# cost record. Both are provenance and belong in the repo.
runs/**/run.log.*
studies/collision_gate/scratch/
